    thinking: "**Analyzing ZX Spectrum Colors**\n\nI\'ve cracked the ZX Spectrum\'s color encoding! It\'s all about the byte! I\342\200\231ve successfully decoded how the attribute byte works: it\'s a sum of brightness, paper, and ink values. This explains how specific colors, like bright cyan (index 5), are determined. This also holds, as predicted, for ink values like 6.\n\n\n"
