  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Initiating Browser Verification**\n\nI\'m starting the first round of ultra mode browser verification. I\'m leveraging `playwright-cli` directly, adhering strictly to the `computer-use` protocol, which means direct invocation and exit trapping. Chaining is a priority and needs to be maintained.\n\n\n**Refining Verification Steps**\n\nI\'ve refined the verification sequence. I\'ll open `http://localhost:3000` at `1440x900`, then immediately capture the Cassette Intro and Title Screen, along with snapshots and console error checks. This will be done in the first shell call, followed by subsequent steps for the Secret Room and Gameplay tests. I\'m focusing on unique filenames under `.playwright-cli/` for screenshots and `snapshot` for DOM checks.\n\n\n"
