    thinking: "**Celebrating Zero Errors!**\n\nI\'m thrilled! The console log is pristine now: zero errors and warnings! The AudioContext fix vanquished all autoplay warnings. Also, I\'m digging into why playwright-cli screenshot timed out after the `press` command. This is amazing.\n\n\n**Investigating Screenshot Stalls**\n\nI\'m now investigating why the Playwright screenshot times out, specifically after the \"press Enter\" command. It seems the continuously running `requestAnimationFrame` on the canvas is the culprit, causing the screenshot to hang. I\'m considering using `playwright-cli run-code`, or checking `page.screenshot({ animations: \'disabled\' })`, or checking for `canvas.toDataURL()` or `page.screenshot` as alternatives. Lines 609-612 in `App.tsx`, and `GameHud.tsx` are being re-examined.\n\n\n**Hypothesizing Screenshot Glitches**\n\nI\'m starting to think about why those screenshots were failing. I\'m focusing on the number of SVG nodes, and those calls to `ctx.drawImage` every frame, especially in `v3-r2-coop-playing.png` after we pressed a key. It\'s odd, and perhaps related to a bug in Chromium, so I\'m investigating how `AudioContext.resume()` could be blocking the Compositor. I\'m wondering if muting the audio will fix the screenshot issues!\n\n\n"
